<title>INDIA: INDIA'S RBI SETS 8-YEAR BOND CUT-OFF AT 11.19 PCT.</title>
<headline>INDIA'S RBI SETS 8-YEAR BOND CUT-OFF AT 11.19 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said it set a cut-off rate of 11.19 percent at an auction of eight year government stock on Monday to raise 30 billion rupees.</p>
<p>The bond was fully subscribed.  </p>
<p>The RBI said it received 466 bids for 98.44 billion rupees of which it accepted 87 (19 of them partial) for 30 billion.</p>
<p>The partial allotment percentage was 61.87 percent.</p>
<p>There was no devolvement on the RBI or the primary dealers.</p>
<p>The weighted average cut-off rate was 11.15 percent.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom (91)-22-265 9000</p>
